<%- include('./partials/header') %>

<%#
 * PLAIN ENGLISH: The Bookings Admin page. Admins see every booking. Everyone
 *   else who is logged in sees only the bookings where they are a passenger.
 *   Each booking can be edited or deleted from here.
 * LOGIC: This page opens EMPTY. It shows "Loading bookings..." first. Then
 *   public/js/bookings-admin.js calls /api/bookings, copies the hidden
 *   template once per booking, fills it in, and shows the list. The Edit and
 *   Delete buttons call PUT and DELETE /api/bookings/:id.
 * WHY WE NEED IT: The Bookings feature (issue #16) created this page.
 *   Feature Set 4 (issue #19) adds login protection, the right list for each
 *   user, and the ability to update and delete bookings.
 * LEARNING GAP: There is no forEach loop over bookings in this file. That is
 *   on purpose. It follows the trains page (src/views/trains.ejs).
 *   Who may open this page is decided by the route lock in
 *   src/routes/ejs-routes.js. Which bookings appear is decided by the
 *   server, not by this page.
 *   These notes are EJS comments, so they never show up in the browser.
 *   An EJS comment cannot contain the EJS closing tag as plain text,
 *   because EJS would think the comment ends there.
 * DATA COMES FROM: Nothing here. The data comes later from /api/bookings.
%>

<section class="bookings-hero">
    <h1>Bookings Admin</h1>
    <p>
        Admins see every booking. Everyone else sees the bookings where they
        are a passenger. Newest bookings are first.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="bookings-catalog">
    <%#
     * PLAIN ENGLISH: The messages the page can show.
     * LOGIC: "Loading" shows first. The error, "no bookings," and action
     *   messages start hidden. The JavaScript shows the right one.
     * LEARNING GAP: role="alert" makes screen readers read the error out
     *   loud. aria-live="polite" reads the other messages when they change.
     *   bookings-message is new for Feature Set 4. It says things like
     *   "Booking KR-AB12CD was deleted" after an edit or delete.
    %>
    <div class="bookings-state" id="bookings-loading" aria-live="polite">Loading bookings...</div>
    <div class="bookings-state bookings-error" id="bookings-error" role="alert" hidden></div>
    <div class="bookings-state" id="bookings-empty" aria-live="polite" hidden>No bookings yet.</div>
    <div class="bookings-state" id="bookings-message" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>

    <div class="bookings-grid" id="bookings-list"></div>

    <%#
     * PLAIN ENGLISH: The hidden pattern for one booking card.
     * LOGIC: The browser does not show a template. The JavaScript copies it
     *   once for each booking and fills in each data-field spot.
     * LEARNING GAP: The top of each card is a div, not a header tag. The
     *   site already styles every header tag as the green page banner, so a
     *   header tag here made the booked date hard to read on a green bar.
     *   The passenger list starts empty because a booking can have one
     *   person or many. The JavaScript adds one line per passenger.
    %>
    <template id="booking-card-template">
        <article class="booking-card">
            <div class="booking-card-header">
                <h2 data-field="code"></h2>
                <span class="booking-date" data-field="created"></span>
            </div>

            <dl class="booking-specs">
                <div class="spec-item">
                    <dt>Trip</dt>
                    <dd data-field="trip"></dd>
                </div>
                <div class="spec-item">
                    <dt>Schedule</dt>
                    <dd data-field="schedule"></dd>
                </div>
                <div class="spec-item">
                    <dt>Travel Day</dt>
                    <dd data-field="day"></dd>
                </div>
                <div class="spec-item">
                    <dt>Ticket Class</dt>
                    <dd data-field="ticket-class"></dd>
                </div>
            </dl>

            <div class="booking-passengers">
                <h3>Passengers (<span data-field="passenger-count"></span>)</h3>
                <ul data-field="passengers"></ul>
            </div>

            <%#
             * PLAIN ENGLISH: The Edit and Delete buttons for this booking.
             * LOGIC: data-action tells the JavaScript which button was
             *   clicked. type="button" stops the button from submitting a
             *   form by accident.
             * WHY WE NEED IT: Feature Set 4 asks for the ability to update
             *   and delete bookings from this page.
             * LEARNING GAP: Showing these buttons is not the security. The
             *   server checks every PUT and DELETE and sends 403 if the
             *   user is not a passenger and not an admin.
            %>
            <div class="booking-actions" data-field="actions">
                <button type="button" class="booking-button" data-action="edit">Edit</button>
                <button type="button" class="booking-button booking-button-delete" data-action="delete">Delete</button>
            </div>

            <%#
             * PLAIN ENGLISH: The edit form for this booking. It stays hidden
             *   until the Edit button is clicked.
             * LOGIC: The ticket class choices come from /api/ticket-classes.
             *   The days are written here. The passenger boxes are added by
             *   the JavaScript, one group per passenger.
             * LEARNING GAP: "required" makes the browser ask for missing
             *   names before sending. The server still checks too, because
             *   anyone could send a request without using this form.
            %>
            <form class="booking-edit-form" data-field="edit-form" hidden>
                <label>
                    Ticket Class
                    <select name="ticketClass" data-field="edit-ticket-class" required></select>
                </label>

                <label>
                    Travel Day
                    <select name="selectedDay" data-field="edit-day" required>
                        <option value="monday">Monday</option>
                        <option value="tuesday">Tuesday</option>
                        <option value="wednesday">Wednesday</option>
                        <option value="thursday">Thursday</option>
                        <option value="friday">Friday</option>
                        <option value="saturday">Saturday</option>
                        <option value="sunday">Sunday</option>
                    </select>
                </label>

                <fieldset class="booking-edit-passengers">
                    <legend>Passengers</legend>
                    <div data-field="edit-passengers"></div>
                </fieldset>

                <p class="booking-edit-error" data-field="edit-error" role="alert" hidden></p>

                <div class="booking-actions">
                    <button type="submit" class="booking-button">Save</button>
                    <button type="button" class="booking-button" data-action="cancel">Cancel</button>
                </div>
            </form>
        </article>
    </template>
</section>

<script src="/js/bookings-admin.js" defer></script>
<%- include('./partials/footer') %>
